"OverallSummary": "This case involves ACP Securities' failure to disclose on its Form CRS that one of its associated persons had disciplinary history from July 2021 to January 2024. The firm employed an individual in June 2021 who had disciplinary history, including using a non-firm-approved communications platform to communicate with a customer regarding firm business. Despite this information being available through FINRA's Central Registration Depository and BrokerCheck, ACP Securities continued to respond 'no' to the question 'Do you or your financial professionals have legal or disciplinary history?' on its Form CRS until January 4, 2024, when it finally amended the form. This constituted a willful violation of Exchange Act § 17(a)(1), Exchange Act Rule 17a-14, and FINRA Rule 2010. As a result, ACP Securities was censured and fined $20,000. This case does not involve Care Obligation violations but rather relates to regulatory reporting requirements. The impact is that retail investors receiving the firm's Form CRS during this period would have received inaccurate information about the disciplinary history of the firm's financial professionals."
